{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2380,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The search for a single number,\n the Hubble constant,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5500,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the rate of expansion of our universe,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...has consumed astronomers for generations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10320,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, two powerful\n and independent methods..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...have refined its measurement\n to unprecedented precision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16760,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only problem...\n is that they don't agree,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19920,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and it's causing to question..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21500,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...some of the most basic assumptions\n about the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29220,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1929, Edwin Hubble...\n discovered the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33480,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He gave us\n our first incontrovertible proof..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that there are galaxies\n outside the Milky Way,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39280,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...by measuring the distances\n to the spiral nebulae"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42840,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were many millions\n of light years from us,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45280,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...far outside the Milky Way, \nand so must be galaxies in their own right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49660,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Combined with the Doppler shift\n velocity measurements of Vesto Slipher,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53420,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...Hubble revealed that the galaxies\n are not only receding from us,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56620,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...but they are receding at a rate\n proportional to their distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59900,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An impossibly vast universe\n had been discovered beyond the Milky Way,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63800,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and at the same time\n that universe was revealed to be expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67480,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The galaxies appear to be racing away from us,\n because the intervening space is expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72380,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We encapsulate the expansion of the universe\n with a single number, called the Hubble constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78040,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "H-naught  (H0)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79420,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It tells us how fast the galaxies appear to be\n retreating from us, dependent on their distance apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85080,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, more fundamentally, H0 tells us\n the rate of expansion of the universe..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89520,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...in the modern era."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91380,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ever since Hubble's great discovery,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93540,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the search for H0\n has been the all-consuming obsession..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97320,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...of thousands of astronomers\nacross the generations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100600,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, understandably,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102240,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the rate of expansion of the universe,\n combined with the gravitational effect..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105820,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...of the matter and energy it contains,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107980,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...can be used to determine\n its entire expansion history,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111460,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...from the Big Bang to its final fate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's fundamental for interpreting\n our observations of the distant universe,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118760,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...whose light has traveled billions of years\n through this expanding cosmos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122500,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can imagine the alarm\n when the two most powerful methods..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125820,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...used to measure this fundamental parameter,\n the Hubble constant,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129440,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...gave different results!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130900,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before we get to that, let's talk about\n the great quest to measure the Hubble constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135800,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until the new millennium, the best we could do\n was to estimate H0 within a factor of 2,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141460,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "... somewhere between 50 and 100\nkilometers per second per megaparsec."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146260,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These strange units\n warrant some explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149240,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Km/s, that's for\n the recession speed of a given galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153200,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Megaparsecs is for its distance,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155520,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...with 1 megaparsec being\n around 3.3 million light-years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159420,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the Hubble constant were, say,\n 75 km per second per megaparsec,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164140,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...then for every 1 mega parsec distance,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...we'd expect the galaxy to be retreating from us\n at an additional 75 kilometers per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171800,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Historically,\n measurement of the Hubble constant..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174180,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...meant measuring the recession velocity and distance\n for as many galaxies as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179200,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The velocity part is relatively easy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just do as Vesto Slipher did,\n and measure redshift."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185400,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the lengthening of the wavelength \nof light from that galaxy,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189300,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...which was stretched as it travels to us\n through an expanding universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193900,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The distance...\n that's tricky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196360,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hubble used Cepheid variables,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198840,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...giant stars, \n during the last phases of their lives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202020,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They pulsate with a period..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203820,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that's related to their true brightness,\n as discovered by Henrietta Leavitt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207720,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Measuring Cepheid periods in other galaxies\n gave Hubble their true brightnesses,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212160,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...as though undimmed by distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214440,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cepheids became what we call \"standard candles\",\n objects of known luminosity,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219180,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...whose observed brightness, therefore,\n tells us their distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222720,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this calculation\n involves assumptions and uncertainties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226120,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For one thing, the Cepheid\n period-luminosity relationship..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229840,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...first had to be calibrated,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231500,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...based on nearby Cepheids,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233200,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...whose distances can be figured\n using stellar parallax"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237100,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tracking their tiny motions on the sky,\n as Earth orbits the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This stepwise determination of astronomical distances\n is called the cosmic distance ladder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247040,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With each step on the ladder,\nuncertainties compound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250600,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Add this to our uncertainties in the behavior and observation of Cepheids themselves,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and the precise measurement\n of the Hubble constant..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257640,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...has been a slow laborious process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260320,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As larger telescopes\n and more expansive surveys were completed,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263860,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...we gradually whittled down\n the errors in H0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266920,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An important advance was \nthe development of new standard candles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270780,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cepheids are good, but can only be seen\n out to a certain distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274960,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Supernovae can be seen much further,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278020,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and type 1a supernovae are the key."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281120,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These result when white dwarfs,\n ancient remnants of dead stars,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285500,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...absorb too much material\n from a binary partner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288620,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Runaway fusion\n causes them to detonate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291720,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The resulting explosion\n has highly predictable brightness,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295180,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...making them\n excellent standard candles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297540,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1990s,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299060,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...astronomers were using these supernovae\n to better nail down the Hubble constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303500,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They inadvertently discovered..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305340,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that the expansion of the universe\n is actually accelerating,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308580,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...revealing the existence of dark energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311300,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the Nobel Prize winning researchers\n  behind this discovery is Adam Riess."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316280,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Riess has continued the quest..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318240,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...to refine our measurement of H0\n to ever greater precision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321680,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big part of his work is to improve the calibration\n of type 1a supernovae as standard candles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327380,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Riess's Supernovae H0 for the Equation of State\n project, - SHOES -,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332080,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...uses the Hubble Space Telescope\n to match old supernovae observations..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336160,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...with new, more reliable Cepheid variables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By improving this run\n on the cosmic distance ladder,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341880,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...all past supernovae distances\n also improve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344980,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Recent teams have now narrowed down the Hubble constant to 73.5 ± 1,7..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351380,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...kilometers per second per megaparsec"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353520,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That 2%-ish uncertainty..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355740,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...is a hell of a lot better\n than the old factor of 2 uncertainty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359780,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, where's the crisis?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361960,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in order to fully believe\n a measurement like this,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364640,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...we prefer it to be made\n through independent methods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367620,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The SHOES project measures the recession of galaxies\n up to around 2 billion light years away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372520,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's a more or less direct measurement\n of the CURRENT expansion rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377620,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's another way to go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379300,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if we could measure the expansion rate\n of the universe at the very beginning?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, we could figure out what its current expansion rate should be, given our best understanding..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388400,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...of all the gravitational influences\n that affected that expansion since the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393700,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, we'd better hope\n that it does give the same result,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...or there is a big problem,\n with either our supernova measurements..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...or with our understanding\n of how the universe evolved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Spoiler: ...\n there IS a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's another reason to try to calculate H0 from observation of the early universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412240,
    "dDurationMs": 6220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's that that observation I'm referring to\n is far more reliable than Cepheids and supernovae."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418460,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm talking about the\n Cosmic Microwave Background radiation, the CMB."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423440,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a topic we've been over,\n so, for now, just the TLDR."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427080,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Cosmic Microwave Background is the remnant\n heat glow of the universe's initial hot dense state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432760,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Released around 400,000 years\n after the Big Bang,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435700,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...when the universe had finally cooled down enough\n to become transparent to light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439680,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We still see it today,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441220,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...now stretched by a factor of 1,100\n by its near 14 billion year journey..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446240,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...through an expanding universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448800,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the map of the CMB across the entire sky,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452560,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...created by the Planck satellite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454740,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The speckles are\n tiny differences in temperature,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457900,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...corresponding to tiny\n differences in density."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460980,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The blue regions are a factor of 100,000\n cooler than the red regions,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466400,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and also slightly more dense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468680,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These over-densities..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470160,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...would go on to collapse into the vast\n clusters of galaxies of the modern universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474820,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So,...  how can the CMB\n tell us the Hubble constant?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478200,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The key is\n the sizes of those speckles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481400,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the era just before the release of the CMB,\n matter and light were trapped together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486760,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Matter wanted to collapse\n under its own gravity,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489360,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...while light generated a powerful pressure\n to resist that collapse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493140,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These counteractive forces\n produced oscillations,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496960,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...really vast sound waves\n that rippled across the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500840,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are\n the baryon acoustic oscillations,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503880,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and they occurred\n on all different sized scales,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506400,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...sloshing between high and low density,\n over those 400,000 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511160,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the release of the CMB meant that light and matter\n were no longer coupled together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516480,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so those oscillations stopped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The state of the oscillations\n at the moment of that release..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522040,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...is imprinted on the CMB,\n in those speckles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We usually show\n the distribution of speckle sizes..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527520,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...with what we call a power spectrum,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529880,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...which basically shows the abundance\n of speckles of different sizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533520,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The location of these peaks..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535540,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...tells us which oscillation modes..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537540,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...just happened to be at their peaks..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539780,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...at the moment the CMB was released."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This, in turn, depends\n on the density of matter and radiation,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545840,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...as well as the expansion rate\n of the universe in that early epoch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549700,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, how do you get the Hubble constant,\n i.e., the current expansion rate, from all of this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555100,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, first you figure out\n what starting cosmological parameters..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558160,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...could give the power spectrum\n observed by Planck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561140,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those parameters include the starting combination\n of both dark and light  matter, and radiation,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566340,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...as well as the initial expansion rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568600,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569320,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...you figure out how the universe\ndescribed by these parameters..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572260,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...should evolve to the present day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574360,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This sounds involved,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575660,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...but the Planck power spectrum is so rich\n with information, that the Planck team..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579900,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...claim to have calculated H0\n with even better precision than SHOES."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584660,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is,\n the results don't agree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587240,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Planck H0 is 66.9 ± 0.6\n kilometers per second per megaparsec,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593400,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...compared to the supernova result\n of 73.5 ± 1.7."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598580,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, they're actually\n remarkably close,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600540,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...given we figured them out\n from data at the opposite ends of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604640,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they also seem\n irreconcilably different,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608020,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...3,7 sigma different in fact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610460,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means a 1/7000 chance..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613620,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that that level of difference\n could have happened through random errors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617140,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the crisis in cosmology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620120,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This discrepancy first emerged in 2016, when\nRiess's new calibration of the supernova-derived H0..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626000,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...revealed it to be in real conflict\n with the Planck result from a couple of years earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630940,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since then, calibrations have been improved,\n results have been rechecked,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635120,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and independent methods have been used\n to calibrate the supernovae as standard candles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640300,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The difference is real,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and, in fact, \nthe error bars are only getting smaller."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646000,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, before we declare\n all cosmology broken,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649540,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...let's think about the two main possible sources\n of this discrepancy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653380,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First: there are unknown\n systematic sources of uncertainty..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657400,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...in either the supernova\n or Planck measurements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660320,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Biases, that are driving one or the other\n to be too high or too low."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665300,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps we don't understand\n Cepheid variables like we thought,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668460,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...or perhaps gravitational lensing alters the \nPlanck speckles differently to how we thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673480,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ongoing efforts are ruling out\n systematic errors one by one,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677760,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...but it's possible there's still something\n we haven't thought of yet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681180,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second:  there's some unknown physics..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684180,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that needs to be taken into account\n for the CMB calculation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688160,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the most exciting possibility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690880,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are a few options."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692680,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's start a new list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694840,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One:  A new type\n of very fast-moving particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698400,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Insufficient numbers could skew the energy balance\n of the early universe, and mess up the calculation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That particle could be\n the sterile neutrino,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708240,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...a hypothetical, non-interacting neutrino,\n that isn't part of the standard model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713220,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two:  Dark matter particles\n behave differently to how we thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717420,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps dark matter interacts more strongly\n with matter and radiation,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721320,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...which would shift the sizes\n of those CMB speckles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725100,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three:  Dark energy isn't constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728680,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The current calculations assume that dark energy\n is described by the cosmological constant,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733860,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...which, by definition,\n doesn't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736140,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if dark energy increases,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738180,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that could explain why we observe\n a higher H0 in the modern universe..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...than is predicted by extrapolating\n from the early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746200,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer will depend on whether the more\n correct measurement of the Hubble constant..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750580,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...comes from Planck or SHOES."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753120,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New observations and new telescopes\n will refine these numbers even further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757540,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Independent methods, like using\n gravitational lensing, or gravitational waves,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762440,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...will weigh in on one side or the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764760,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps the uncertainties will be refined,\n and the two results will converge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769300,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That'd be cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The near centennial quest to measure\n the expansion rate of the universe will be concluded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775880,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or perhaps the discrepancy will persist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779080,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would be even cooler"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780740,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'll have a new tool..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782100,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...to investigate the mysterious physics\n of dark energy, dark matter,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785860,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...or of unknown particles\n beyond the standard model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788560,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For now, we continue\n our obsessive quest for H0..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792780,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and for what it'll tell us\n of the origin and fate of our expanding space-time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799520,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In today's comment responses,\n we need to catch up on 2 episodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803320,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, it's our journal club\n on Dr. Jamie Farnes' paper..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806880,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...about negative mass dark fluid..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...as a unifying explanation\n of both dark matter and dark energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812760,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we'll get to comments\n on our CPT symmetry episode."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, a friend of a friend\n of Dr. Farnes' chimed in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820280,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leo Staley's friend says that Dr. Farnes\n doesn't necessarily believe the claims of his paper,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826480,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...but rather its purpose\n was to spark interesting ideas among physicists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, okay.   I totally respect that motivation\n to publish even quite fringe ideas,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836040,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and he certainly\n sparked a conversation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838460,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, look,\n I'm still talking about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841060,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Andrew Paulfreyman points out that..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843100,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the gravitational lensing measurements\n of dark matter..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846040,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...will give the exact opposite results\n if dark matter is due to this negative mass fluid..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851020,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...than if it's actual,\n positive mass matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854780,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And my intuition tells me\n that this is right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858220,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravitational lensing\n is the bending of light by a gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862260,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We see it in the warping\n of images of distant objects,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...due to the gravitational fields\n of more nearby galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can use that warping\n to measure masses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872960,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yeah, those measures tell us\n that dark matter has positive mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877500,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd need to do the simulations,\n but I have a feeling..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880820,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...that we wouldn't even see\n this sort of strong gravitational lensing..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884820,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...if the effect of dark matter\n was due to this dark fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Marik Zilberman's\n distaste for negative masses..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891400,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...is that they produce perpetual motion machines\n and paradoxes left and right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895740,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly what I thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897260,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a theory leads to these - sort of - \npathological predictions, it's a big red flag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902320,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we're actually going to do\n a challenge question episode,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905080,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...to explore these paradoxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907220,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stay tuned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908500,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, let's move on to our episode\n on the ultimate symmetry of nature,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the simultaneous reversal\n of charge, parity, and time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917320,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First up:  a few of you asked questions\n about time reversal, so I want to clarify."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The T in CPT symmetry\n isn't a literal rewinding of the clock."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927800,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's best thought of\n as a reversal of all motion,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931220,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...both linear and angular momentum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934180,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything reverses direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936340,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the universe has\n this sort of T symmetry,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...then, if you reverse all motion,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941000,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...the universe will evolve exactly backwards,\n to its initial state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945380,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turns out that's not the case,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947580,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...as demonstrated by the different forward/backward reaction rates in certain quantum interactions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954220,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the universe IS symmetric\n under full CPT inversion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959260,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, a CPT inverted universe\n is not the same as this universe,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963680,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...but the laws of Physics are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965980,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The point is that you can't tell\n which of the two you're in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969760,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "TinyFox Tom asks whether mass\n would be inverted under CPT symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974840,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I guess you're referring to the idea\n that time-reversed energy has its sign flipped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980880,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the simple answer is no,\n because the T in CPT isn't a true time reversal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986760,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the case of a true time reversal,\n the answer is, essentially, yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991620,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a negative mass particle,\n moving backwards in time,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994640,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...is mathematically the same as a positive mass particle moving forward in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999400,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That notion makes sense in the math,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001840,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and is used in, for example, Feynman's\n path integral formulation of quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007180,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's not so obvious whether this idea\n corresponds to anything physical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012100,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rishit Vora asks how a T inversion\n would affect a black hole?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017180,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, a true time reversal\n that included the interior of a black hole..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021540,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...should transform it into a white hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024260,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything that ever fell in\n would come rushing out,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027240,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...and presumably reassemble itself into\n the stars, spaceships, monkeys,...  that originally fell in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033660,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As to the motion reversal symmetry\n of the T in CPT,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037960,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...frankly, I'm not sure, because we don't know\n the state of matter in the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043200,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, at any rate, remember\n that T symmetry is broken."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047000,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both the T of CPT\n and true time reversal symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051140,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a rewound black hole shouldn't revert exactly\n to whatever it formed from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056000,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That doesn't mean\n information is lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058200,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just that it ends up\n in a different form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060640,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And back to dark fluid for a sec."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062620,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mr. Nation [?] has his own unified theory\n of the Dark Sector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066600,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He reveals to us\n that dark energy equals dark matter,..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070260,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...times the speed of dark..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071740,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...squared.\n[  DE  =  dm•(cd^2)  ]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073340,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Genius on so many levels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075620,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only scientific levels,\n but still, levels."
    } ]
  } ]
}
